  "label": "Suffering victims are mapped onto a 'tough project'",
  "description": "The text 'this project is tough but it will save the world' is juxtaposed with the visual of emaciated, dying victims. The mapping equates the extreme suffering and death of the victims with the difficulty of a project, implying that the project's hardship is comparable to or justified by the victims' suffering. This is an analogical mapping where the visual material (suffering victims) is mapped onto the textual concept (a tough project).",
